{"questions":[{"question_id":"1l23irmod","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline","year":2012,"examDate":2012,"subject":"chemistry","chapter":"gaseous-state","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","topic":"real-gas-and-van-der-walls-equation","type":"mcq","marks":3,"negMarks":1,"permalink":"pfor-one-mole-of-a-van-der-waals-gas-when-b--0-and-t--30-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-qcq6zrgwkotyej6x","content":"<p>For one mole of a van der Waals gas when b = 0 and T = 300 K, the PV vs. 1/V plot is shown below. The value of the van der Waals constant a (atm L<sup>2</sup> mol<sup><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.186ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1.76ex\" height=\"1.505ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -583 778 665\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>2</sup>) is</p>\n<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Gaseous State Question 10 English\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l24lf9pp/1b49bd1c-0106-4eef-940f-99088eea51e3/f7aac0e0-bf04-11ec-8fbf-67f2639a0a45/file-1l24lf9pq.p